// Pi-SDK ⇄ assistant-ui bridge.
//
// Holds live Pi AgentSessions (one per assistant-ui thread), and exposes them over
// HTTP + SSE. Pi stays the source of truth; on every Pi event we re-project the
// session's authoritative state into assistant-ui `ThreadMessageLike[]` and push a
// snapshot to subscribed SSE clients. This makes the React side a thin
// ExternalStoreRuntime and gives history/resume for free (the first SSE frame on
// (re)connect is the full snapshot).
//
// Endpoints:
//   GET  /api/health
//   GET  /api/sessions                      -> thread list
//   POST /api/sessions                      -> { id } (new thread)
//   GET  /api/sessions/:id/events           -> SSE snapshot stream
//   GET  /api/sessions/:id/messages         -> snapshot (one-shot)
//   POST /api/sessions/:id/prompt           -> { message, images?, streamingBehavior? }
//   POST /api/sessions/:id/abort
//   GET  /api/commands                      -> slash commands (prompt/skill/extension)
//   GET  /api/files?q=                      -> file list for @-mentions
//   GET  /api/sessions/:id/artifacts        -> this session's downloadable files (under .artifacts/<id>/)
//   GET  /api/sessions/:id/artifacts/download?path= -> stream one artifact (attachment, realpath-guarded)
//   GET  /api/daily/latest.csv              -> the nightly call list (one stable bookmarkable URL)
//   GET  /api/daily/latest.xlsx             -> the same list as a two-sheet workbook, born at the response edge
//   GET  /api/nightly                       -> the night's ready-made handover files (home-view strip)
//   GET  /api/nightly/download?name=        -> stream one nightly file (attachment, realpath-guarded)
//   GET  /api/models                        -> available models
//   POST /api/sessions/:id/model            -> { provider, modelId }
//   POST /api/sessions/:id/thinking         -> { level }
//   GET  /api/sessions/:id/stats            -> token/cost/context
//   POST /api/sessions/:id/feedback         -> { messageId, kind, value } (sidecar JSONL)

